
export anchor Story_38491dd3c805ec7f:
    userPrompt:
        \\\
        While the body's Planning tab is selected, neither sidebar shows. Planning then
        fills the whole width of the window beneath the ribbon, from the window's left edge
        to its right, and from the tab bar down to the bottom.

        The left sidebar is hidden whole, view bar and all. This is an exception to
        spec/ui/components/left-sidebar/index.pi#LeftSidebar.description and
        spec/ui/components/left-sidebar/index.pi#LeftSidebar.viewBar ("The bar is always
        there"). The right sidebar doesn't show either, even while a task runs, the queue
        holds a prompt, or it was opened by hand. This is an exception to
        spec/ui/components/right-sidebar/index.pi#RightSidebar.showing, and the body's
        right-sidebar button and Ctrl+Alt+B (Cmd+Alt+B on macOS) do nothing while Planning
        is selected.

        This works like the chat input, which already hides while Planning is selected, as
        spec/scope/application/Body.pi#Body.tabs says: both sidebars go at once with nothing
        sliding, and come back at once when Chat, a file or a task tab is selected. They
        come back as they were left: the left sidebar's view, collapsed state, width,
        scroll and selection, and the right sidebar's width and whether it was opened by
        hand. If a task started or ended while Planning was showing, the right sidebar comes
        back in whatever state that leaves it.

        Update spec/scope/application/Body.pi#Body.description and
        spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.description so Planning is placed across the
        full window width.
        \\\

    mode: combined

    model: opus
